  "details": "See this post, as this SDK also affects Unity 2019: https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/1116-some-materials-on-avatars-appearing-black-in-parts-of-the-world\n\nI used 2021.07.12 of the Live version of SDK3 to find this bug while running the live Unity 2018 version of VRChat. \nI uploaded this as a Build & Test avatar, but have also created a public upload for anyone to look into (avtr_cce787bf-e342-48ed-9b64-60486ff71fc2). It's using the Unity-chan shaders that come with the avatar, but changing it to another shader makes it look normal.\n\nThe legacy upload of Unity-chan on the avatar menu looks fine, but I have suspicion that this is an SDK bug.",
